  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 226 AM CDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nA mid/upper ridge continues to dominate the weather over the region \nwith the center of the H5 ridge located over the Ohio Valley area \nearly this morning. Meanwhile, the low level thermal ridge was \nsituated across the Central Plains and this is expected to persist \nthough the upcoming week. As we move into Friday and Saturday, the \nmid/upper ridge is progged to retrograde and build back over the \nCentral Plains once again. Much above normal temperatures are \nexpected to persist across the area over the upcoming 7 days \nwith minimal chances for meaningful precipitation. Uncertainty \nbegins to increase as we move into the Tue-Wed timeframe. A \nrobust shortwave trough racing eastward across southern Canada \nmay drive a frontal boundary southward into the Central Plains. \nConfidence in this scenario remains fairly low at this time with\nconsiderable uncertainty in the southward extent of the \neffective front.",
